# A tilt error is a phase-matching error at the design wavelength: the peak moves to another wavelength.
# Reference: closed form with complex error functions.
title Fibre tilted +4 degrees from the emission angle
grating angle=10 length=30
leak 0.14
fibre angle=14
sweep 1.45 1.65 401
expect radiated 0.98500442 1e-06
expect overlap 0.22711976 2e-05
expect efficiency 0.11185698 2e-05
expect position 2.42808617 0.005
expect peak_wavelength 1.50466269 0.0002
expect bandwidth_1db 41.55287497 0.004
expect bandwidth_3db 72.99220203 0.004
